{"id":"n-20261028-o2qe16","category":"business","display_title":"Global Markets and Local Currency","display_title_he":"השווקים הגלובליים והמטבע המקומי","short_summary":"Global chip stocks surged following stellar earnings from SK Hynix and major AI infrastructure funding, while the Israeli shekel weakened amid political uncertainty after the elections.","english_level":"C1","words":433,"reading_time":3,"image":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/BHT_6_-_Global-local_concerns%2C_average_across_the_surveyed_markets%2C_sixth_wave_compared_with_fifth_wave.png/960px-BHT_6_-_Global-local_concerns%2C_average_across_the_surveyed_markets%2C_sixth_wave_compared_with_fifth_wave.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","credit":"SOworu (WMF) · CC BY 4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:BHT_6_-_Global-local_concerns,_average_across_the_surveyed_markets,_sixth_wave_compared_with_fifth_wave.png"},"sources":[{"name":"Globes","domain":"globes.co.il","url":"https://www.globes.co.il/news/article.aspx?did=1001561013","title":"מצב השווקים: SK Hynix דיווחה על רבעון שיא ושולחת את סיאול לעליות חדות","published_at":"2026-10-28T06:26:00.000Z"}],"published_at":"2026-10-28T06:26:00.000Z","first_published_in_app_at":"2026-10-28T06:57:48.288Z","quality_score":9,"interest_score":9,"verification_status":"verified","content_status":"published","paragraphs":["Global financial markets experienced notable movements recently, driven by stellar corporate earnings, massive artificial intelligence investments, and political developments. According to reports, South Korean chip manufacturer SK Hynix announced record-breaking third-quarter financial results that substantially surpassed analyst expectations. The company generated revenues of $78.86 billion and an operating profit of $62.82 billion, marking massive year-over-year growth compared to the previous period. Alongside this financial milestone, SK Hynix declared plans to allocate over $25 billion toward dividends and share buybacks. This exceptional performance sent the Seoul stock exchange surging by more than 6%, bolstered by significant jumps in both SK Hynix and Samsung shares, which together account for about 50% of the total market capitalization in South Korea.","Meanwhile, Wall Street maintained a positive momentum, supported by developments surrounding artificial intelligence infrastructure and upcoming technology earnings, following the filing of a prospectus by Anthropic. Broadcom gained significant attention after major financial institutions, including Bank of America, Blackstone, Citi, and Morgan Stanley, established a special purpose vehicle to finance $63 billion worth of Broadcom artificial intelligence chips for Anthropic. This massive backing prompted analysts at D.A. Davidson to upgrade Broadcom and raise their price target significantly to $400, reflecting strong optimism regarding the semiconductor supply chain. Concurrently, investors prepared for upcoming interest rate decisions from the Federal Reserve, expecting rates to remain steady at 4%, and crucial quarterly reports from tech giants like Microsoft and Alphabet, where market participants anticipated robust cloud revenue growth.","In local markets, the Israeli shekel reacted sharply to election exit poll results that pointed toward a potential political deadlock without a clear governing majority. Following the initial projections, the shekel weakened by approximately 1% against the US dollar, trading around 3.08 shekels per dollar and erasing earlier gains recorded during the voting day. Financial researchers from the Tel Aviv Stock Exchange noted that historical election patterns from 2003 to 2022 typically involve short-term volatility and a dip during the first week, followed by a recovery over the course of the following month as market participants gain clarity regarding economic policy and government formation.","Institutional investment shifts also caught the attention of market observers. Regulatory filings with the SEC revealed that investment giant BlackRock increased its holdings in chip foundry Tower to 6.8%, making it a prominent shareholder. Conversely, BlackRock trimmed its position in Nova from roughly 7.1% down to 4.9%, falling below the reporting threshold for major stakeholders. Additionally, investment bank Jefferies adjusted its price target for Check Point Software to $185 while maintaining a buy rating, noting that despite potential near-term sales challenges and earnings pressure, the valuation remains defensive as the company approaches the upcoming year with a projected P/E multiple of 11."],"facts":[{"fact":"SK Hynix reported record third-quarter results, surpassing analyst expectations and sending Seoul stocks surging over 6%.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"BlackRock reduced its stake in Nova to 4.9%, dropping below the major shareholder threshold, while increasing its stake in Tower to 6.8%.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Jefferies raised its price target for Check Point to $185 while maintaining a buy rating, anticipating potential pressure after upcoming earnings.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Following election exit polls indicating potential political gridlock without a clear majority, the Israeli shekel weakened sharply by about 1% against the dollar to around 3.08.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Major investment banks established a special purpose vehicle to finance $63 billion of Broadcom AI chips for Anthropic.","sources":[1]}],"glossary":[{"text":"Global","lemma":"global","pos":"adj","he":"גלוֹבָלִי","name":""},{"text":"financial","lemma":"financial","pos":"adj","he":"פִינַנְסִי","name":""},{"text":"markets","lemma":"market","pos":"n","he":"שְׁוָוקִים","name":""},{"text":"experienced","lemma":"experience","pos":"v","he":"חָווּ","name":""},{"text":"notable","lemma":"notable","pos":"adj","he":"בּוֹלֵט","name":""},{"text":"movements","lemma":"movement","pos":"n","he":"תְּנוּעוֹת","name":""},{"